#: ../../../reference/interfaces/desktop-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/desktop-interface.md:8
msgid "desktop interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/desktop-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"`desktop` allows access to basic graphical desktop resources, such as "
"Wayland."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/desktop-interface.md:12
msgid "**Auto-connect**: yes</br> **Attributes**:</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/desktop-interface.md:12
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/desktop-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"`desktop-file-ids` (plug): optional, list of desktop file ids with valid D-"
"Bus well-known names (e.g. `[org.example, org.example.Foo]`). This would "
"indicate that the snap would like to install desktop file(s) named "
"`org.example.desktop` and `org.example.Foo.desktop` (found under `meta/gui`) "
"without name mangling (ie, without the snap name prefix) (requires *snapd "
"2.66*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/desktop-interface.md:17
msgid ""
"The `desktop` slot is {ref}`unsupported for parallel instances <interfaces-"
"parallel-installs-unsupported>`. The `desktop` plug is supported for "
"parallel instances only if it does not set `desktop-file-ids`."
msgstr ""
